    "physical_description": "Bag Face, hand-knotted woollen pile on woollen warp and weft; Central Asia, Beluch; 19th century.\r\n\r\nWARP: white wool; Z2S; 16 threads per inch (64 per dm).\r\n\r\nWEFT: dark brown wool; Z2S; 2 shoots after each row of knots; 9 knots per inch (39 per dm).\r\n\r\nPILE: wool; 7 colours: dark red, red, very dark green, dark blue, blue, dark brown, white; asymmetrical knot open to the left and tied around 2 threads; 72 knots per sq.inch (1248 per sq.dm).\r\n\r\nSIDE FINISH: 2 cords overcast with brown wool.\r\n\r\nEND FINISH: cut. Lower end has 0 .75\" (2 cms) plainweave with dark brown weft decorated in red and white and dark brown complimentary weft float. Upper: 0.5\" (1.5 cms)plainweave with dark brown weft with one band of red and brown complimentary weft-wrapping.\r\n\r\nDESIGN: Field: dark brown ground divided into four by thin red and blue lines from an 8-pointed star in reds and blue, outlined in brown and then dark blue.  On the horizontal bar on both sides are two pairs on inward-facing horns and on the vertical, angular lines suggesting a floral sprig. In each quarter there is a dark blue stylized tendril.  The ground has red and white florets scattered over it.\r\n\r\nMain Border: dark blue ground with octagonal guls similar to the central one, outlined in either red/blue/red or white.dark blue/brown.  On the sides, a red square separates each gul and a line of small, floral guls frames each larger motif.  Along the lower and upper borders the main motifs are seaparted by pairs of similar small guls each joined by a striped bar.\r\nInner and Outer borders: white ground with an angular meander in which the main elements are a stylized blue and red S-motif and red triangular leaves.  In the lower right hand corner there are tiny red and white flowerheads.\r\n\r\nDate Catalogued: 11.12.96",
